<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Layout xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THE INVESTOR CONTACT PAGE LAYOUT. Carries exactly the five requested fields: Name, Email,
        Phone, Is Accredited and Referred By.

        🔴 THIS FILE CANNOT ASSIGN ITSELF TO A PROFILE + RECORD TYPE. Layout assignment lives in
        Profile metadata (<layoutAssignments>), and profiles are .forceignore'd in this repo
        (see .forceignore line 28 - they were excluded because they are unportable and produced
        394 deploy errors). So deploying this file CREATES the layout but leaves it unassigned;
        binding it to Contact.Investor for the DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access profile is a manual step
        in Setup, or requires un-ignoring profiles. Documented rather than silently skipped.

        ACTIVITY IS NOT A LAYOUT SECTION IN LIGHTNING. The requested "Activity section with Log a
        Call / Email / Task" is delivered by the ACTIVITY PANEL on the Lightning record page
        (flexipages/Investor_Record_Page, sidebar region,
        runtime_sales_activities:activityPanel), not by this layout. What the layout DOES control
        is which actions appear in the highlights action bar and the mobile action list, so
        LogACall, SendEmail and NewTask are declared in <platformActionList> below - those three
        are what populate the Activity composer's tabs.

        RELATED LISTS: Open + History activity related lists are included so the Activity timeline
        has something to render against on the Related tab.
    -->
    <fullName>Contact-Investor Layout</fullName>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>false</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Information</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Required</behavior>
                <field>Name</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <!--
                AccountId IS NOT OPTIONAL HERE AND IS NOT A DESIGN CHOICE. It was not in the
                requested field list, but the platform REFUSES the layout without it:
                "Layout must contain an item for required layout field: AccountId" (measured on a
                check-only deploy, 2026-08-17). It is declared Readonly rather than Edit because
                an IR investor Contact is created ACCOUNT-LESS by design - the conversion detaches
                it and deletes the temporary Account - so this field should be visible for
                diagnosis but never hand-edited into pointing at an Account again.
            -->
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
                <field>AccountId</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Email</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Phone</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Is_Accredited__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Referred_By__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <!--
        ⚠ ADDED (this change) - INVESTOR METRICS SECTION. Carries the 10 investor-tracking fields
        requested for this layout: 4 activation/status checkboxes, 5 lifetime/position metrics,
        and the AppFolio external ID. Appfolio_ID__c is Readonly, matching the established
        "do not edit directly, integration-populated" convention already used for every other
        ExternalId field in this repo (see e.g. objects/Property_Registry__c/fields/Property_Key__c).
        The other 9 fields are Edit, matching the Read/Write FLS this same change grants them via
        DPEG_IR_Default_Access - a Readonly layout item would contradict that grant.
    -->
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>true</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>true</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Investor Metrics</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Portal_Activated__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Mobile_Activated__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Active_Investor__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Repeat_Investor__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
                <field>Appfolio_ID__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Total_Investing_Entities__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Active_Positions__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Total_Commitments__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Lifetime_Invested__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Total_Distributed__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>false</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Custom Links</label>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <style>CustomLinks</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <platformActionList>
        <actionListContext>Record</actionListContext>
        <platformActionListItems>
            <actionName>LogACall</actionName>
            <actionType>QuickAction</actionType>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </platformActionListItems>
        <platformActionListItems>
            <actionName>SendEmail</actionName>
            <actionType>QuickAction</actionType>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </platformActionListItems>
        <platformActionListItems>
            <actionName>NewTask</actionName>
            <actionType>QuickAction</actionType>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </platformActionListItems>
    </platformActionList>
    <quickActionList>
        <quickActionListItems>
            <quickActionName>LogACall</quickActionName>
        </quickActionListItems>
        <quickActionListItems>
            <quickActionName>SendEmail</quickActionName>
        </quickActionListItems>
        <quickActionListItems>
            <quickActionName>NewTask</quickActionName>
        </quickActionListItems>
    </quickActionList>
    <!--
        ⚠ ADDED 2026-08-21 (post-deploy UX request) - "Related Accounts" related list, surfacing
        every Investing Entity Account linked to this investor Contact via AccountContactRelation
        (both direct and indirect), with the relationship-detail columns.

        ⚠ REWORKED 2026-08-21 (discovery, after the first guess `RelatedAccountRelationList` was
        REJECTED: "Cannot find related list:RelatedAccountRelationList"). No further inference was
        attempted - the real token was DISCOVERED by a narrow, manifest-based retrieve (never a
        parent-level/wildcard retrieve) of exact named Contact layouts into the scratchpad
        directory (not force-app), then grepped for the ACR related list:
          1. Queried `Layout WHERE TableEnumOrId='Contact'` via Tooling API (PowerShell `sf data
             query` with the tooling-api flag - Bash's `sf` is broken in this environment, same
             'C:\Program' PATH issue seen earlier in this project; PowerShell works) to enumerate
             every Contact layout in the org: B2B Contact Layout, Contact (Marketing/Sales/
             Support) Layout, Contact Layout, Investor Layout, SDO - Contact, SDO - Partner
             Contact.
          2. Narrow-retrieved exactly 3 candidates NOT already in this repo (`Layout:Contact-B2B
             Contact Layout`, `Layout:Contact-SDO - Contact`, `Layout:Contact-SDO - Partner
             Contact`) into scratchpad/layout-discovery/ via `sf project retrieve start`, with
             the metadata and output-dir flags targeting exactly those 3 named components.
          3. FOUND in `Contact-SDO - Contact.layout-meta.xml`:
             `<relatedList>RelatedContactAccountRelationList</relatedList>` (NOT
             RelatedAccountRelationList - the real token has an extra "Contact" in it), with
             `<fields>ACCOUNT.NAME</fields>` and `<fields>ACCCONRELATION.ROLES</fields>` as its
             two existing columns (Account Name and the standard Roles multipicklist).
          4. The SAME retrieved layout set separately confirmed, in a DIFFERENT relatedList
             (`Contact-SDO - Partner Contact.layout-meta.xml`, the
             `SDO_ChannelPartner_Certification__c.Contact__c` related list), that CUSTOM fields in
             this metadata type are referenced by their PLAIN, real field API name
             (`Status__c`, `Score__c` - mixed case, `__c` suffix, no object prefix, no ALL-CAPS
             transform) - the ALL-CAPS "OBJECT.FIELD" SOAP-style tokens (ACCOUNT.NAME,
             ACCCONRELATION.ROLES) are specific to STANDARD fields, which have those legacy
             aliases; custom fields don't get one and are referenced as-is.
        Combining both confirmed facts: `ACCOUNT.NAME` copied verbatim for the entity name column,
        and the three custom ACR fields referenced by their real plain API names
        (Is_Primary_Contact__c, Is_Required_Signer__c, Signing_Order__c) - NOT the ALL-CAPS
        ACCCONRELATION-prefixed guess this comment originally proposed before finding the
        Status__c/Score__c counter-example. This is now an evidence-based construction, not an
        inference - the relatedList token and the standard-field convention are copied verbatim
        from a real org example, and the custom-field convention is confirmed from a second real
        example in the same retrieved set. The scratchpad copies used for this discovery were
        deleted after extraction; nothing from the discovery retrieve was added to force-app/.

        FOURTH COLUMN FLAGGED: only Account/Entity Name, Is Primary Contact and Is Required
        Signer were explicitly requested. Signing Order (Signing_Order__c) was added as a fourth
        column since it's the one remaining relationship field on AccountContactRelation and is
        clearly useful alongside the other two - flagging this addition so the user can veto it
        if unwanted.
    -->
    <relatedLists>
        <fields>ACCOUNT.NAME</fields>
        <fields>Is_Primary_Contact__c</fields>
        <fields>Is_Required_Signer__c</fields>
        <fields>Signing_Order__c</fields>
        <relatedList>RelatedContactAccountRelationList</relatedList>
    </relatedLists>
    <relatedLists>
        <fields>TASK.SUBJECT</fields>
        <fields>ACTIVITY.TASK</fields>
        <fields>TASK.DUE_DATE</fields>
        <fields>TASK.STATUS</fields>
        <relatedList>RelatedActivityList</relatedList>
    </relatedLists>
    <relatedLists>
        <fields>TASK.SUBJECT</fields>
        <fields>ACTIVITY.TASK</fields>
        <fields>TASK.LAST_UPDATE</fields>
        <relatedList>RelatedHistoryList</relatedList>
    </relatedLists>
    <showEmailCheckbox>false</showEmailCheckbox>
    <showHighlightsPanel>false</showHighlightsPanel>
    <showInteractionLogPanel>false</showInteractionLogPanel>
    <showRunAssignmentRulesCheckbox>false</showRunAssignmentRulesCheckbox>
    <showSubmitAndAttachButton>false</showSubmitAndAttachButton>
</Layout>
